  "id": "psychiatric-pharmacogenomics",
  "term": "psychiatric pharmacogenomics",
  "definition": "Psychiatric pharmacogenomics is the use of genetic information to help tailor medication choices in psychiatry. It mainly studies how gene variants affect drug handling in the body and, less consistently, treatment effects, with the strongest current evidence involving certain antidepressants and some antipsychotics.",
